{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"**Rule 6c-11:** An AP must be a participant in a registered clearing agency and have a written agreement with **the ETF or one of its service providers** permitting creation-unit purchases and redemptions. The rule does not require the distributor to be the counterparty.\n\n**US contractual pattern:** The main signatories are commonly the **AP and distributor**. The trust may be an expressly protected **third-party beneficiary**, rather than a signatory; other forms make it a party. Those statuses should not be conflated.\n\n**Irish ICAV contrast:** The ICAV is a corporate fund, not a trust. Its AP arrangement can make the **ICAV itself, its manager and the AP** contracting parties.\n\nThe referenced forms are not available here, so I cannot verify their particular signatories or beneficiary provisions.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Regulatory permission to contract is distinct from who actually signs and can enforce an agreement."}}
